cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenFAWE, please cite the archived release below rather than the repository URL."
title: "OpenFAWE: an open framework for coupled floating airborne wind energy dynamics and physics-linked cost screening"
abstract: >-
  OpenFAWE is an open-source, time-domain framework for the offshore engineering side of
  Floating Airborne Wind Energy (F-AWE): how a floating station and its lines respond when a
  crosswind-flying airborne unit acts on them as a moving, direction-varying boundary condition,
  and what the resulting design envelopes cost. It couples an airborne-wind lifting-surface /
  free-vortex-wake module with potential-flow hydrodynamics in a Cummins time-domain model, two
  configurations of a lumped-mass line model, and turbulent inflow. Design-basis load envelopes
  are carried through line and anchor sizing into manufacturing-stage CAPEX and comparative
  levelised cost of energy, with computed and assumed cost drivers reported separately. OpenFAWE
  does not aim to advance airborne-wind flight physics, kite design or flight-control synthesis;
  those inputs are taken from the published state of the art and frozen in the design basis.
